to "defective" until a row in `docs/ops/shutdown-compliance.md`
records the verification.

## Why this rule has `alwaysApply: true`

Push-triggered CI was deliberately removed (see `ci-policy.mdc`).
The agent, the per-crate clippy lints, and the shared
`pim-shutdown` crate are the three enforcement surfaces. This
rule must be loaded into every conversation so the agent's first
instinct on adding any new binary — or editing the shutdown path
of an existing one — is to install the handler, wire the drain,
and update the compliance doc, not to "wire it up later".
